en.math:
\begin{aligned}
I
&=
\int dt\,
\left[
-m\sqrt{1-\dot{\mathbf x}^{\,2}}
-eA_\mu\frac{dx^\mu}{dt}
\right]
\notag\\
&=
\int dt\,
\left[
-m\sqrt{1-\dot{\mathbf x}^{\,2}}
-e\left(A_0+A_m\dot x^m\right)
\right].
\end{aligned}

p.src:
Choose one spatial component $x^m$. Differentiating the free term of  gives $\frac{m\dot x_m}{\sqrt{1-\dot{\mathbf x}^{\,2}}}
=
m u_m,
\qquad
u^\mu\equiv\frac{dx^\mu}{d\tau}.$ The first board attempt stops there. An audience correction catches the omission: the interaction term also depends on $\dot x^m$. The complete derivative is $\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot x^m}
=
\frac{m\dot x_m}{\sqrt{1-\dot{\mathbf x}^{\,2}}}
-eA_m
=
m u_m-eA_m.$

