p.src:
Consider the massless scalar equation in one spatial dimension, $\frac{\partial^2\phi}{\partial t^2}
-\frac{\partial^2\phi}{\partial x^2}
=0,$ obtained from $\mathcal L_0
=
-\frac12\partial_\mu\phi\,\partial^\mu\phi.$ If $\phi$ is a solution, then so is $\phi\longrightarrow\phi+c,$ where $c$ is constant. Every derivative of $c$ vanishes, so neither the equation nor the derivative-only Lagrangian changes.

